  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": true,
    },
    "description": "Execute a planned blueprint. Requires server:apply and an unexpired preview token from
discord_server_blueprint_plan bound to this blueprint revision, guild, and guild snapshot.

Discord has no transactions, so every action is journalled before it runs. A partial failure
returns what completed, what failed and why, and what was not attempted — and already-created
objects are bound immediately, so re-planning after a fix will not duplicate them.
Deleting managed objects additionally requires mcp:destructive.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "auditLogReason": {
          "maxLength": 512,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "blueprintId": {
          "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$",
          "title": "blueprint id",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "deleteManaged": {
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "guildId": {
          "description": "A Discord ID: 17-21 decimal digits, always a string.",
          "examples": [
            "123456789012345678",
          ],
          "pattern": "^\\d{17,21}$",
          "title": "Snowflake",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "previewToken": {
          "type": "string",
        },
        "revision": {
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "blueprintId",
        "guildId",
        "previewToken",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "discord_server_blueprint_apply",
    "title": "Apply a blueprint to a guild",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    "description": "Compare a published blueprint revision against a guild and return an ordered diff. This never
mutates Discord.

Reports blockers at plan time rather than mid-apply: a role at or above the bot’s highest, a
permission the bot does not hold and so cannot grant, a channel whose type cannot be converted.
Reapplying a converged blueprint yields zero actions. Unmanaged resources are never touched.

Returns a preview token bound to the blueprint revision AND the current guild snapshot, so a
stale plan cannot be applied. Requires server:plan.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "blueprintId": {
          "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$",
          "title": "blueprint id",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "deleteManaged": {
          "description": "Allow deletion of objects this blueprint marks absent. Off by default; applying deletions also requires mcp:destructive.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "guildId": {
          "description": "A Discord ID: 17-21 decimal digits, always a string.",
          "examples": [
            "123456789012345678",
          ],
          "pattern": "^\\d{17,21}$",
          "title": "Snowflake",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "revision": {
          "description": "Defaults to the latest published revision.",
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "blueprintId",
        "guildId",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "discord_server_blueprint_plan",
    "title": "Plan a blueprint against a guild",
  },
